# Research Quality Standards

Design for skeptical peer review, not confirmation.

## Causal checks (before any finding)
- **Tautology**: predicting Y with a restatement of Y (or post-outcome info) is a mirror — dig for the upstream cause
- **Confounder**: if A beats B, control what else differs; if the effect vanishes after stratification, it was spurious correlation
- **Fair compare**: only rank entities in the same comparability group; state the group
- **Actionability**: "there is a correlation" is not a finding — name mechanism + recommended action
- **Proxy variables**: labels (region, org type) stand in for latents — name the mechanism or caveat

## Pre-registration & controls
- State hypotheses before runs; label exploratory work as exploratory
- Every experiment needs a null baseline; change one variable at a time

## Stats & reporting
- Effect sizes + CIs, not vibes; exact p-values; Bonferroni when multi-testing
- Pin versions/seeds; log raw data; YAML config committed with results
- Report nulls and surprises; plots need error bars; every number traces to a script
